1
00:01:51,111 --> 00:02:02,351
I'm saying no one can fix her not even us no way we we've gone everywhere without any problems

2
00:02:02,351 --> 00:02:08,151
until now in theory even if we did everything we could the probability of your ship lasting

3
00:02:08,151 --> 00:02:13,031
till the next island is zero

4
00:02:21,111 --> 00:02:29,751
Mary tell me it's what he said true you'll never sail again

5
00:02:29,751 --> 00:02:37,791
pirate abduction incident and a pirate ship that can only await her end

6
00:02:37,791 --> 00:02:49,551
this sucks I'm sorry Sonji I was so focused on the books that I didn't notice when she left

7
00:02:49,551 --> 00:02:54,651
there's nothing you should have to apologize for I just assumed that the person I saw walking with

8
00:02:54,651 --> 00:03:01,331
Robin had to have been you and your human form which begs the question who was that masked man

9
00:03:01,331 --> 00:03:07,951
and how were they able to disappear so suddenly yeah even Robin's scent disappeared

10
00:03:07,951 --> 00:03:18,551
I hope everything's all right I feel uneasy do you need an examination no that's not what I meant

11
00:03:18,551 --> 00:03:25,951
it's what Aokiji said his words keep repeating what did he say that worries you it was all that

12
00:03:25,951 --> 00:03:31,731
terrible stuff he said about Robin's past and then very soon we'd regret her being on our crew

13
00:03:31,731 --> 00:03:36,851
oh yeah right so do you think what he said might have had something to do with her disappearance

14
00:03:36,851 --> 00:03:43,091
I don't know but I know we're getting nowhere looking for her let's head back to the ship for now

15
00:03:43,091 --> 00:03:49,871
if nothing's wrong she'll come back on her own eventually yeah you're right hurry back to the Mary

16
00:03:49,871 --> 00:03:53,871
what

17
00:03:53,871 --> 00:04:21,271
What?! You can't fix the going, Mary?! Why not?!

18
00:04:21,271 --> 00:04:25,871
I thought all of you were supposed to be awesome shipwrights!

19
00:04:25,871 --> 00:04:28,771
Don't worry about the money! Look, we got plenty!

20
00:04:28,771 --> 00:04:32,371
It's not about the money, son.

21
00:04:32,371 --> 00:04:38,171
No matter how much you pay, that ship can't be restored to how she used to be.

22
00:04:38,171 --> 00:04:42,671
To be honest, I'm rather impressed you were able to get that old girl this far,

23
00:04:42,671 --> 00:04:45,071
considering the condition that she's currently in.

24
00:04:45,071 --> 00:04:48,671
What's that supposed to mean?! What exactly is going on with the Mary?!

25
00:04:48,671 --> 00:04:51,671
Do you know what the keel is, immoral girl?

26
00:04:51,671 --> 00:04:54,671
Immo- The thing at the bottom of the boat?

27
00:04:54,671 --> 00:04:58,271
Yeah. It's the most important piece of lumber on a ship.

28
00:04:58,271 --> 00:05:02,671
It crosses from stem to stern and provides support.

29
00:05:02,671 --> 00:05:06,071
When you build a ship, you start off by placing the keel.

30
00:05:06,071 --> 00:05:11,871
Then you set the wood for the stem, the stern, the frame, frame brackets and deck beams.

31
00:05:11,871 --> 00:05:18,271
All of the pieces are carefully assembled together, with the keel serving as the core.

32
00:05:18,271 --> 00:05:22,371
It's the very backbone, framework and life of every vessel constructed.

33
00:05:22,371 --> 00:05:25,671
And when it's severely damaged, then that's the end of her.

34
00:05:25,671 --> 00:05:27,971
You can't just replace it with a new one.

35
00:05:27,971 --> 00:05:32,471
That'd be the same thing as building a new ship from scratch.

36
00:05:32,471 --> 00:05:36,271
That's the reason we, or anyone, won't be able to fix her.

37
00:05:36,271 --> 00:05:39,771
Your ship's just a bunch of wood stuck together, awaiting her end.

38
00:05:39,771 --> 00:05:42,071
Hey you! Don't say such horrible things!

39
00:05:43,571 --> 00:05:45,571
Horrible or not, it's the truth.

40
00:05:45,571 --> 00:05:53,671
Okay, fine then. Just rebuild her from the ground up, like you said before. Build another Going Mary.

41
00:05:53,671 --> 00:05:56,671
Cuckoo! Sorry, not possible.

42
00:05:56,671 --> 00:05:57,671
Why not?

43
00:05:57,671 --> 00:06:03,171
We could build you a very similar ship, but no one can build you one that would be exactly the same.

44
00:06:03,171 --> 00:06:07,671
Nowhere in the world are there two completely identical ships. It simply can't be done.

45
00:06:07,671 --> 00:06:09,071
What do you mean? Why?

46
00:06:09,071 --> 00:06:12,971
Tell me, are there any trees in the world that grow exactly the same way?

47
00:06:12,971 --> 00:06:20,771
A sailing ship is mostly built out of lumber, so the overall size and shape of a vessel is determined by the type of wood used.

48
00:06:20,771 --> 00:06:27,071
That's why an exact duplicate of your ship can't be built by us or anyone, even when using the same blueprints.

49
00:06:27,071 --> 00:06:31,871
If we made a ship like that with those specifications, the ones who would notice the difference,

50
00:06:31,871 --> 00:06:38,071
and feel that it's a completely different ship, would be all of you guys! Cuckoo!

51
00:06:38,071 --> 00:06:44,371
No way! So you're saying it's absolutely impossible for us to continue sailing on the Going Mary?

52
00:06:44,371 --> 00:06:51,871
Unfortunately, yes. You can either wait around for her to sink, or you can dismantle her immediately.

53
00:06:51,871 --> 00:06:54,371
A real Carabelle!

54
00:06:54,371 --> 00:06:59,371
What a cool ship! Have you guys seen the front? It's totally awesome!

55
00:06:59,371 --> 00:07:06,671
Okay! It's all done! Now the Going Mary has everything she could possibly need!

56
00:07:06,671 --> 00:07:13,171
Well, your ship is on her last legs. Why don't you look at this as an opportunity?

57
00:07:13,171 --> 00:07:17,171
You happen to be in the best place in the world to buy a new ship. You have money, right?

58
00:07:17,171 --> 00:07:25,171
I understand that your ship was a Carabelle. Sailing on the Grand Line in an old ship like that would be difficult to begin with.

59
00:07:25,171 --> 00:07:27,971
No way! We're not getting a new ship!

60
00:07:27,971 --> 00:07:28,971
Luffy...

61
00:07:28,971 --> 00:07:30,971
The Mary is...

62
00:07:30,971 --> 00:07:36,971
The Going Mary is the ship of the Straw Hat Pirates! If she's repaired, then she can still sail!

63
00:07:36,971 --> 00:07:40,971
She'll be fine! You'll see! She got us here today, didn't she?

64
00:07:40,971 --> 00:07:45,971
And you tell us out of nowhere she can't sail anymore? I can't believe that! I won't!

65
00:07:45,971 --> 00:07:50,971
You guys are saying that because you don't know her! You have no idea how strong she is!

66
00:07:50,971 --> 00:07:58,771
Then your plan is to keep sailing her until she sinks? I'm shocked!

67
00:07:58,771 --> 00:08:04,771
So, this is the decision of the ship's captain?

68
00:08:04,771 --> 00:08:12,771
This discussion is over for now. Just think about it. If you decide to buy a ship, let me know. My people can help.

69
00:08:12,771 --> 00:08:18,571
If you're able to spend $300 million, we can build a state-of-the-art ship for you. Califa?

70
00:08:18,571 --> 00:08:25,571
Here. If you'd look this over, please. It's a catalog of our new and our used models. Use it as a price reference.

71
00:08:25,571 --> 00:08:31,571
Hey, Iceberg! There's someone at the front gate who wants to see you. Hmm?

72
00:08:31,571 --> 00:08:35,371
There doesn't seem to be anyone on your appointment schedule for today.

73
00:08:35,371 --> 00:08:40,371
It looks like those world government officials again. Should I tell them you're unavailable?

74
00:08:40,371 --> 00:08:41,371
Well...

75
00:08:41,371 --> 00:08:47,371
Yes, please. Say I'm gone. By the way, Lulu, you've got quite a case of bedhead.

76
00:08:47,371 --> 00:08:51,971
Oops! How embarrassing. My apologies. Anyway, I'll ask them to leave.

77
00:08:51,971 --> 00:08:53,971
Uh, thanks. I appreciate it.

78
00:08:53,971 --> 00:08:57,371
Hold it right there, Iceberg. Hmm?

79
00:08:57,371 --> 00:09:03,171
Looks like you're here after all.

80
00:09:03,171 --> 00:09:06,171
Hey, you two need to hide. Government officials are here.

81
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:09,171
What? Uh, okay.

82
00:09:13,171 --> 00:09:17,171
Well, hello again, Corgi. As you can see, I'm not here today.

83
00:09:17,171 --> 00:09:24,171
Yes, you are. Come now. I've come all the way out here by sea train. Don't turn me away. It's impolite.

84
00:09:24,171 --> 00:09:34,971
For some reason, I detect the scent of pirates.

85
00:09:34,971 --> 00:09:38,971
Whatever. In any case, I want to talk to you.

86
00:09:38,971 --> 00:09:40,971
I don't like you. Go away.

87
00:09:40,971 --> 00:09:42,971
Are you a child?

88
00:09:42,971 --> 00:09:44,771
Uh-uh. I'm totally an adult.

89
00:09:46,771 --> 00:09:48,771
Then start acting like one.

90
00:09:48,771 --> 00:09:51,771
There's something of special importance I need to discuss with you.

91
00:09:51,771 --> 00:09:53,771
I would appreciate it if you'd hear me out.

92
00:09:55,771 --> 00:09:57,771
Come. Let's talk this over in private.

93
00:10:00,771 --> 00:10:02,771
Those government guys are so damn persistent.

94
00:10:02,771 --> 00:10:05,771
What the hell do they want with Iceberg anyway?

95
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:09,571
Look, it has nothing to do with us. Probably political stuff.

96
00:10:10,571 --> 00:10:11,571
Should I beat them up?

97
00:10:11,571 --> 00:10:14,571
I wouldn't. I mean, they're government guys after all.

98
00:10:19,571 --> 00:10:21,571
What? What's wrong?

99
00:10:21,571 --> 00:10:25,571
Something seemed weird about these bags when I grabbed them.

100
00:10:27,571 --> 00:10:29,571
They're really light.

101
00:10:29,571 --> 00:10:31,571
Huh? What do you mean?

102
00:10:31,571 --> 00:10:32,371
What do you mean?

103
00:10:34,371 --> 00:10:36,371
Oh, come on. Stop kidding around.

104
00:10:36,371 --> 00:10:39,371
How could they be with all of that money inside?

105
00:10:45,371 --> 00:10:46,371
Hey, who's that?

106
00:10:46,371 --> 00:10:47,371
What's with the screaming?

107
00:10:49,371 --> 00:10:51,371
Idiots! What the hell are you...

108
00:10:51,371 --> 00:10:52,371
Hot lady!

109
00:10:52,371 --> 00:10:55,371
If you sit like that, everyone can see your...

110
00:10:57,371 --> 00:10:58,371
Don't tell me.

111
00:10:58,371 --> 00:11:00,171
There's no way.

112
00:11:01,171 --> 00:11:03,171
I don't want to look.

113
00:11:06,171 --> 00:11:08,171
200 million!

114
00:11:08,171 --> 00:11:10,171
Gone! It's really gone!

115
00:11:10,171 --> 00:11:12,171
Wait, look at these bags! They're not even ours!

116
00:11:14,171 --> 00:11:15,171
What are we going to do?

117
00:11:15,171 --> 00:11:17,171
Hey, hey! Keep it down!

118
00:11:17,171 --> 00:11:18,171
What's wrong?

119
00:11:18,171 --> 00:11:21,171
Our money. Our money's gone.

120
00:11:21,171 --> 00:11:24,171
Finished. Got disappeared.

121
00:11:24,171 --> 00:11:25,171
What?

122
00:11:25,171 --> 00:11:26,171
Holly, was it you again?

123
00:11:26,171 --> 00:11:27,171
Huh? No!

124
00:11:27,171 --> 00:11:28,971
Honest?

125
00:11:28,971 --> 00:11:29,971
Why would I lie?

126
00:11:29,971 --> 00:11:30,971
You mean it?

127
00:11:30,971 --> 00:11:31,971
Yes, I mean it.

128
00:11:31,971 --> 00:11:32,971
They're so noisy.

129
00:11:32,971 --> 00:11:33,971
Hey, Kaku, question for you.

130
00:11:33,971 --> 00:11:36,971
Why were you hanging out with the Frankie family earlier?

131
00:11:36,971 --> 00:11:37,971
What are you talking about?

132
00:11:37,971 --> 00:11:41,971
I haven't been anywhere near a single member of the Frankie family all day.

133
00:11:41,971 --> 00:11:42,971
That's strange.

134
00:11:42,971 --> 00:11:43,971
Huh.

135
00:11:43,971 --> 00:11:46,971
I was so certain that I saw your long nose.

136
00:11:46,971 --> 00:11:47,971
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

137
00:11:47,971 --> 00:11:48,971
Hold on a sec!

138
00:11:48,971 --> 00:11:49,971
That's Usa!

139
00:11:49,971 --> 00:11:52,971
You saw him with the Frankie family?

140
00:11:52,971 --> 00:11:54,771
Well, you could say he was with them.

141
00:11:54,771 --> 00:11:56,771
Or maybe you could say he was being dragged away.

142
00:11:56,771 --> 00:11:58,771
That's called kidnapping!

143
00:11:58,771 --> 00:12:00,771
Loopy, we gotta find him!

144
00:12:00,771 --> 00:12:03,771
Hey, hold on!

145
00:12:03,771 --> 00:12:04,771
Where are you going to look?

146
00:12:04,771 --> 00:12:09,571
Wait for me, Usaq!

147
00:12:09,571 --> 00:12:11,571
Wait for me, Money!

148
00:12:11,571 --> 00:12:12,571
I'm coming!

149
00:12:15,571 --> 00:12:18,571
Hey, where can I find the Frankie family's hideout?

150
00:12:18,571 --> 00:12:19,571
It's not really a hideout.

151
00:12:19,571 --> 00:12:21,571
It's more like a workshop.

152
00:12:21,571 --> 00:12:25,571
From where your ship is docked, it's way up the seashore to the northeast.

153
00:12:25,571 --> 00:12:26,571
It's off by itself.

154
00:12:26,571 --> 00:12:28,571
You can't miss it.

155
00:12:28,571 --> 00:12:32,371
It's called the Frankie House.

156
00:12:48,371 --> 00:12:50,371
Loopy!

157
00:12:50,371 --> 00:12:52,371
Loopy!

158
00:12:52,371 --> 00:12:55,371
What was he thinking?

159
00:12:55,371 --> 00:12:59,171
There's no way he could find Usaq in this place all by himself.

160
00:12:59,171 --> 00:13:01,171
I can't keep looking for him right now.

161
00:13:01,171 --> 00:13:04,171
Before I do anything else, I need to take this money back to the ship.

162
00:13:04,171 --> 00:13:08,171
If I march in there demanding our 200 million back while holding 100 million,

163
00:13:08,171 --> 00:13:10,171
I'd be asking them to steal that money, too.

164
00:13:10,171 --> 00:13:13,171
Yagra, please take me to the bull shop.

165
00:13:13,171 --> 00:13:14,171
Shortest route possible.

166
00:13:21,171 --> 00:13:24,171
I'll take Zoro and the others with me and teach them a lesson.

167
00:13:24,171 --> 00:13:25,971
Stealing from pirates?

168
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:28,971
Frankie family, that makes you the lowest of the low!

169
00:13:34,971 --> 00:13:37,971
First floor, Backstreet Shopping District.

170
00:13:37,971 --> 00:13:39,971
Please proceed with caution.

171
00:13:39,971 --> 00:13:41,971
Thank you and have a wonderful day!

172
00:13:45,971 --> 00:13:47,971
Hurry, I'm counting on you!

173
00:13:49,971 --> 00:13:51,971
What's her problem?

174
00:13:51,971 --> 00:13:53,771
Hey!

175
00:13:53,771 --> 00:13:54,771
Watch where you're going!

176
00:13:54,771 --> 00:13:55,771
I'm sorry, sir!

177
00:13:57,771 --> 00:14:00,771
I hope Usaq was able to escape from them, somehow.

178
00:14:00,771 --> 00:14:15,571
This is terrible!

179
00:14:15,571 --> 00:14:16,571
Where's this guy from?

180
00:14:16,571 --> 00:14:17,571
Hey!

181
00:14:17,571 --> 00:14:18,571
Does anybody know him?

182
00:14:18,571 --> 00:14:19,571
Who is he?

183
00:14:19,571 --> 00:14:20,571
What's with them?

184
00:14:20,571 --> 00:14:21,571
Yagra, wait!

185
00:14:21,571 --> 00:14:22,571
Hold on a second!

186
00:14:22,571 --> 00:14:23,071
Stop!

187
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:23,571
Stop!

188
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:24,371
Usaq!

189
00:14:34,371 --> 00:14:35,371
Hey!

190
00:14:35,371 --> 00:14:36,371
Say something!

191
00:14:36,371 --> 00:14:37,371
Are you alright?

192
00:14:37,371 --> 00:14:38,371
Open your eyes!

193
00:14:38,371 --> 00:14:39,371
Usaq!

194
00:14:39,371 --> 00:14:40,371
Hey!

195
00:14:40,371 --> 00:14:41,371
Usaq!

196
00:14:41,371 --> 00:14:42,371
Wake up!

197
00:14:42,371 --> 00:14:45,371
Excuse me, but are you two pirates by any chance?

198
00:14:45,371 --> 00:14:46,371
Shut up!

199
00:14:46,371 --> 00:14:48,371
Stop scaring and mind your own business!

200
00:14:48,371 --> 00:14:50,171
Oh no!

201
00:14:50,171 --> 00:14:51,171
Usaq!

202
00:14:51,171 --> 00:14:52,171
I did this to you!

203
00:14:52,171 --> 00:14:53,171
Was it the Frankie family?

204
00:14:57,171 --> 00:14:58,171
It was!

205
00:14:58,171 --> 00:15:01,171
It happened because I'm weak!

206
00:15:02,171 --> 00:15:03,171
They took...

207
00:15:03,171 --> 00:15:05,171
They took all the money!

208
00:15:07,171 --> 00:15:08,171
Nabi!

209
00:15:08,171 --> 00:15:18,971
How can I face the others now?

210
00:15:18,971 --> 00:15:26,971
We were finally able to fix the fairy!

211
00:15:26,971 --> 00:15:32,971
I'm so ashamed!

212
00:15:32,971 --> 00:15:36,971
Damn it!

213
00:15:36,971 --> 00:15:39,771
Usaq, I understand.

214
00:15:39,771 --> 00:15:41,771
Don't worry about the money.

215
00:15:41,771 --> 00:15:43,771
We'll get it back together.

216
00:15:43,771 --> 00:15:45,771
He's been beaten pretty badly.

217
00:15:45,771 --> 00:15:47,771
I probably shouldn't move him.

218
00:15:47,771 --> 00:15:51,771
Look, stay right here, okay?

219
00:15:51,771 --> 00:15:54,771
I'm gonna go back to the ship to get the others to come and help.

220
00:15:54,771 --> 00:15:57,771
Chopper will have you fixed up good as new in no time.

221
00:15:57,771 --> 00:16:00,771
And listen, don't worry about the stolen money, alright?

222
00:16:00,771 --> 00:16:03,771
From what I've heard, their hideout isn't too far away from here.

223
00:16:03,771 --> 00:16:06,771
We'll crush them and that'll be the end of it, okay?

224
00:16:06,771 --> 00:16:08,571
Hey!

225
00:16:08,571 --> 00:16:10,571
You think this is some kind of show?

226
00:16:10,571 --> 00:16:11,571
Get lost!

227
00:16:11,571 --> 00:16:13,571
Stay put, okay?

228
00:16:13,571 --> 00:16:15,571
I'm going to get you some help.

229
00:16:15,571 --> 00:16:17,571
I'll be right back!

230
00:16:17,571 --> 00:16:19,371
Let's go!

231
00:16:19,371 --> 00:16:22,371
Okay, let's go!

232
00:16:22,371 --> 00:16:24,371
Hurry, Yakurak, go faster!

233
00:16:24,371 --> 00:16:25,371
Whee!

234
00:16:25,371 --> 00:16:27,371
Ah!

235
00:16:27,371 --> 00:16:28,371
Ah!

236
00:16:28,371 --> 00:16:30,371
Our runaway ball!

237
00:16:30,371 --> 00:16:37,371
We were ugly able to fix the fairy!

238
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:44,331
No matter how much you pay, that ship can't be restored to how she used to be.

239
00:16:45,451 --> 00:16:48,351
Whether we decide to give in and buy a new ship,

240
00:16:49,031 --> 00:16:52,671
or we have someone else manage to fix and improve the Mary,

241
00:16:53,151 --> 00:16:56,191
if we don't put the entire $300 million into this,

242
00:16:56,551 --> 00:16:59,611
our future journeys together will be difficult for sure.

243
00:17:00,691 --> 00:17:04,811
We need that money. All of it. We have to get it back.

244
00:17:07,371 --> 00:17:09,851
What? Is that true?

245
00:17:10,091 --> 00:17:12,191
Well, that's what the shipwright said.

246
00:17:14,691 --> 00:17:15,611
The ship.

247
00:17:16,111 --> 00:17:18,751
It can't be fixed, even if we have money?

248
00:17:19,131 --> 00:17:22,031
Then, then what's going to happen to the Mary?

249
00:17:22,311 --> 00:17:23,011
Beats me.

250
00:17:23,531 --> 00:17:28,051
Honestly, it really just depends on how Luffy and the others react after hearing the assessment.

251
00:17:29,051 --> 00:17:32,411
Either way, I'm sure they'll get it sorted out while they're at the shipyard.

252
00:17:33,091 --> 00:17:36,371
It just seems so extreme. I mean, look at her.

253
00:17:36,371 --> 00:17:38,571
Same old Mary that she's always been.

254
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:43,571
We've traveled together on this ship all the way from the East Blue to this place. Why now?

255
00:17:44,391 --> 00:17:46,171
You just answered your own question.

256
00:17:47,071 --> 00:17:49,931
Human beings become stronger, hardship after hardship.

257
00:17:50,551 --> 00:17:54,031
But ships are different. Their wounds just pile up.

258
00:17:54,031 --> 00:18:04,051
It's so hard to accept. And what is Usopp going to say when he hears about all of this?

259
00:18:04,651 --> 00:18:07,291
I don't want to leave her. I love the Mary.

260
00:18:07,551 --> 00:18:11,871
I know we all do. But her wounds are too deep. There's nothing we can do.

261
00:18:13,871 --> 00:18:16,431
The Mary's in trouble and Robin's still missing.

262
00:18:16,431 --> 00:18:19,671
I'm worried about both of them.

263
00:18:21,551 --> 00:18:22,791
Hey, everyone!

264
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:28,031
Look! It's Nami and she's alone!

265
00:18:28,311 --> 00:18:32,111
Hmm? That's weird. I wonder what happened to Luffy and Usopp.

266
00:18:32,951 --> 00:18:36,171
Hi, Nami! Is everything all right?

267
00:18:36,171 --> 00:18:49,731
What do you think, bro? Awesome, right?

268
00:18:49,731 --> 00:18:52,911
Incredible. You guys are amazing.

269
00:18:53,491 --> 00:18:58,591
Now that we have this much money, we'll be able to get what we've always wanted.

270
00:18:59,151 --> 00:19:00,831
We actually did it, didn't we?

271
00:19:00,971 --> 00:19:04,371
After three years, our perseverance has finally paid off.

272
00:19:04,751 --> 00:19:05,671
I'm stoked!

273
00:19:06,191 --> 00:19:06,851
Me too.

274
00:19:07,091 --> 00:19:10,471
Every time we'd have a little money, we'd bet it all on the Yogg-O'-Races!

275
00:19:11,011 --> 00:19:12,591
And lose every time!

276
00:19:12,951 --> 00:19:16,231
Each time we'd collect a criminal's bounty, we'd party and drink!

277
00:19:16,331 --> 00:19:17,771
And spend it all!

278
00:19:17,771 --> 00:19:21,031
We could never ever save up the 200 million berries that we needed.

279
00:19:21,171 --> 00:19:22,131
Until now!

280
00:19:22,931 --> 00:19:24,991
We finally have enough to get it done!

281
00:19:25,111 --> 00:19:26,011
And then some!

282
00:19:26,471 --> 00:19:27,951
You guys did a hell of a job!

283
00:19:27,951 --> 00:19:35,731
Now then, I know it isn't much, but here's five million berries to show you how grateful I am.

284
00:19:36,131 --> 00:19:37,951
Eat, drink, and have a blast!

285
00:19:42,211 --> 00:19:43,711
That's our bro!

286
00:19:43,811 --> 00:19:44,951
Party time!

287
00:19:52,031 --> 00:19:53,291
What the hell?

288
00:19:53,291 --> 00:19:58,331
What was that?

289
00:19:58,451 --> 00:19:59,511
Show yourself!

290
00:19:59,751 --> 00:20:02,731
What fool would dare to oppose the Frankie family?

291
00:20:02,731 --> 00:20:09,191
Huh?

292
00:20:09,191 --> 00:20:12,131
It's that weakling we ran into earlier!

293
00:20:12,291 --> 00:20:14,091
How did you even manage to stand up?

294
00:20:17,991 --> 00:20:19,611
Give us our money back?

295
00:20:19,851 --> 00:20:21,831
Give us our money back, you say?

296
00:20:22,591 --> 00:20:22,951
Hmm.

297
00:20:23,391 --> 00:20:25,491
Does that mean you're one of the Straw Hats?

298
00:20:25,491 --> 00:20:28,991
That's right, bro, he totally is!

299
00:20:28,991 --> 00:20:33,371
I was expecting all of the Straw Hats crew to be really strong, but this one's not at all!

300
00:20:34,491 --> 00:20:37,071
Yeah, he's a complete weakling, what a joke!

301
00:20:37,191 --> 00:20:38,751
Mind your own damn business!

302
00:20:38,751 --> 00:20:48,191
What's he doing?

303
00:20:48,531 --> 00:20:52,171
You've got some guts trying to take back the money all by yourself.

304
00:20:52,531 --> 00:20:54,831
But I'm afraid I can't let you have it.

305
00:20:58,671 --> 00:21:00,491
Give it back!

306
00:21:00,491 --> 00:21:12,031
We need the money to fix the berry!

307
00:21:16,031 --> 00:21:18,331
Her scars are deep!

308
00:21:21,331 --> 00:21:22,831
That's our money!

309
00:21:22,831 --> 00:21:25,791
It's to heal her wounds, understand me?

310
00:21:26,211 --> 00:21:27,831
You can't have it!

311
00:21:28,571 --> 00:21:30,951
Give it back to me right now!

312
00:21:30,951 --> 00:21:57,131
That's all!

313
00:23:06,184 --> 00:23:11,184
On the next Wood Feast, rescuing our friend, raid on the Frankie House!

314
00:23:11,184 --> 00:23:13,184
I'm gonna be King of the Pirates!

